From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Sep 2024 20:03:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8996-xiaomi-common: Fix TUSB320l
 interrupt polarity

The polarity of the TUSB320l interrupt was incorrectly set to rising edge
instead of falling edge. This didn't cause any issues until the driver started
reading the interrupt polarity from DT in commit
d03a7005d968 ("extcon: usbc-tusb320: Set interrupt polarity based on device-tree")

Change the interrupt flags to fix TUSB320l.

Fixes: 46680fe9ba61 ("arm64: dts: qcom: msm8996: Add support for the Xiaomi MSM8996 platform")
Signed-off-by: Yassine Oudjana <y.oudjana@protonmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-xiaomi-common.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-xiaomi-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-xiaomi-common.dtsi
index 77ad613590..3a74ae93be 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-xiaomi-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8996-xiaomi-common.dtsi
@@ -210,7 +210,7 @@ typec: typec@47 {
 		compatible = "ti,tusb320l";
 		reg = <0x47>;
 		interrupt-parent = <&tlmm>;
-		interrupts = <63 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		interrupts = <63 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
 	};
 };
 
